<title>ISRAEL: Israel June economic performance index up 0.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Israel June economic performance index up 0.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's economic performance or &quot;S&quot; index rose 0.2 percent in June, the Bank of Israel said.</p>
<p>			     June 97   May 97    June 96</p>
<p>Month-on-month change  + 0.2     + 0.8     + 0.3</p>
<p>Index (base 100=1994)  120.7     120.4     117.1</p>
<p>The &quot;S&quot; index is made up of four components: retail sales, which rose 2.6 percent in June; imports, which jumped 6.1 percent in June; industrial production, which gained 2.2 percent in May; and the number of workers, which fell 0.5 oercent in April.</p>
<p>Note: figures for the number of workers and industrial production lag.</p>
<p>Since the beginning of the year the index has increased 3.2 percent, which the Bank of Israel said reflects an expansion in economic activity. In the same period last year the index rose 3.6 percent.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 TCC</p>
</text>
